    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1743">

                <pb facs="1416" n="1300" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1300"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.0145/6.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 506.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">St. Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-03-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 28, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to the Department’s instruction
                    No. 148 of the 11th instant, concerning the Russian law extending to twelve
                    miles from low-water mark the area of supervision by the Russian customs
                    authorities, I have the honor to state that the only information on the subject
                    which the Minister for Foreign Affairs has so far been able to give me was
                    another copy of the Law of December 10/23, 1909 (forwarded with my despatch No.
                    363 of September 30, 1910).</p>
                <p>I have been unable to secure copies of the notes exchanged by the Russian and
                    British Governments on this subject, which is still under discussion, though I
                    had already asked that they be shown for your confidential information.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
